From 60cf122a8a78b6ccd5a92274bffc3cc505ce6cb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:56:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Update base image to Alpine 3.24 and PHP 8.3

Alpine 3.15 reached end of life in November 2023 and its php8 package
is frozen at 8.0.25. PHP 8.0 itself has been end of life since November
2023, so rebuilding the image can no longer pick up security fixes,
including the fixes for CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (PHP2Shell,
remote code execution in PHP-FPM).

Alpine 3.24 ships php83 8.3.36, which contains both fixes. Switch the
php8 packages to php83 (php8-redis is now php83-pecl-redis), move the
PHP config overlay to /etc/php83, and point the supervisor at the
php83 / php-fpm83 binaries and /etc/php83/php.ini. libressl3.4-libssl
no longer exists on Alpine 3.24 and nothing in the image links against
it, so it is dropped.
